  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrating Economic Analysis into Better Regulation: Political Economy Pathways for Institutional Reform in Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The primary objective of this research is to assess the political economy and institutional feasibility of embedding Chief Economist roles or other mechanisms within Indonesian ministries to strengthen regulatory impact assessments (RIAs) and promote evidence-based policymaking. This initiative supports Indonesia&#x2019;s aspirations for OECD accession and aligns with international standards of good regulatory practice. Beyond assessing feasibility, the study aims to illuminate how economic expertise can evolve within Indonesia&#x2019;s existing institutional ecosystem.</narrative>
  </description>
